Feed the sceMpeg decoder stub from the IPU_TO DMA channel (channel 4, 0x1000B400) and report its starvation.

What it fixes: Battle Stadium D.O.N does not give the movie's video stream to sceMpegAddBs. CRI's
Sofdec keeps the raw MPEG-2 video elementary stream in a ring of 2048-byte sectors and sends it to
the IPU through DMA channel 4, in source-chain mode (one ref tag per sector; the last valid sector
ends in a refe tag). The runtime had no channel-4 path, so the stub's sceMpegGetPicture waited
for frames that never came (journal 034).

1. PS2Memory::ipuToPull walks the started chain lazily, one tag payload at a time, advancing
   MADR/TADR/QWC/CHCR as the hardware does, and completes the channel (STR cleared, D_STAT cause 4)
   at the chain end. A CHCR write only sets a "started" flag; a stop clears it and keeps the cursor.
   sceMpegGetPicture pulls 2048 bytes at a time into the decoder until a picture is ready.
2. The end of the movie. libmpeg tells the game's player that the decoder needs bytes through the
   Nodata callback (sceMpegAddCallback type 1; the game registers 0x35D340 with error 0, stop-DMA 2
   and restart-DMA 3). With nothing left the game's callback sets the player's end flag and pushes
   a sequence end, and the player loop (0x36A820) ends. The stub never ran it, so GetPicture
   waited for ever after the last picture. Now, when no picture is ready, bytes were taken from
   channel 4 and the channel is idle, GetPicture queues the registered Nodata callback once per
   amount of data taken (and wakes its own wait when it returns); asked again with nothing new
   it returns without waiting. The CD-stream path is unchanged; other games are affected only if
   they start channel 4 and call sceMpegGetPicture.

How it was verified: tests/runtime/mpeg_ipu_dma_test.cpp (a synthetic 64x32 colour-bar MPEG-2
stream sent through a channel-4 chain: the picture has its size and bar colours, STR is cleared
and D_STAT bit 4 set at the end) passes with the patch and crashes without it (no frame ever
decodes). Game: with DON_PLAY_MOVIES=1 the opening movie plays in the right colours from blank
~1830 to ~6930, the title screen follows by itself and Start opens the main menu; the sound starts
about 1 s after the first picture. The scramble seen with this patch alone was a separate fault
(patch 0065). Depends on patch 0063. Original work; no outside source.

